<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 24,730,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 24,730,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 09/04/96    08/28/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 24,730,000  22,844,000   25,186,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000   33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	    N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 115,544	66,720	    N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   09/04/96    08/28/96    Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,493,000   4,059,000    4,482,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,654,000   4,092,000    4,150,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,618,000   3,545,000    4,905,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,554,000   1,922,000    1,900,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,639,000   3,630,000    3,383,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 3,947,000   3,783,000    4,506,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,824,000   1,813,000    1,860,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	24,730,000  22,844,000   25,186,000</p>
